{"schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"major":0,"minor":3},"seeAlsoSections":[{"title":"How-to Guides","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/HowToAddAPaywall","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/HowToAddAVersionKillswitch","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/HowToAddAParentalGate","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/HowToAddAnalytics","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/HowToAddFeatureFlags","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/HowToAddPersistence","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/HowToAddICloudSync","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/BuildingADomainPlugin","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/AgentSkill"],"anchor":"How-to-Guides","generated":true}],"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/HowToCancelEffects","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"kind":"article","hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux"]]},"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/swidux\/howtocanceleffects"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"metadata":{"modules":[{"name":"Swidux"}],"title":"Cancel Effects","roleHeading":"Article","role":"article"},"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"content","content":[{"type":"heading","text":"Overview","level":2,"anchor":"Overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Every effect the store runs is already cancelled on teardown: "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/Store\/cancelEffects()","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" and the store’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"deinit"},{"type":"text","text":" cancel all in-flight effect tasks. That is enough for cleanup, but it is "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"text":"all-or-nothing","type":"text"}]},{"text":" — you cannot cancel one specific effect while others keep running.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Keyed cancellation adds that. You give an effect a "},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"cancel id","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":" with "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/cancellable(id:cancelInFlight:_:)","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":", and later cancel every effect running under that id with the "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/cancel(id:)","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" effect or the imperative "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/Store\/cancel(id:)","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" method. Identity lives outside the "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/Effect","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" type — it is still a plain closure — so nothing about reducer signatures changes."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Reach for this when an effect outlives the action that started it: cancelling text-to-speech when the user skips, debouncing a search field, or tearing down a long-lived listener when a screen disappears."}]},{"type":"heading","text":"Choosing an id","level":2,"anchor":"Choosing-an-id"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A cancel id is any "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Hashable & Sendable"},{"type":"text","text":" value. Distinct ids are independent; effects sharing an id are cancelled together. A dedicated empty type reads well and can’t collide with another feature’s id:"}]},{"type":"codeListing","code":["private enum SearchID: Hashable, Sendable {}","private enum SpeechID: Hashable, Sendable {}"],"syntax":"swift"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Strings and enums work too — pick whatever is unambiguous in your domain."}]},{"type":"heading","text":"Cancel from inside a reducer","level":2,"anchor":"Cancel-from-inside-a-reducer"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Return "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/cancellable(id:cancelInFlight:_:)","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" to tag the work, and "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/cancel(id:)","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" to stop it:"}]},{"type":"codeListing","code":["case .startSpeaking(let text):","    return cancellable(id: SpeechID()) { send in","        for await word in speech.speak(text) {","            await send(.spokeWord(word))","        }","    }","","case .skip:","    \/\/ Stop any in-flight speech immediately.","    return cancel(id: SpeechID())"],"syntax":"swift"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"When the speaking effect is cancelled, its "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"for await"},{"type":"text","text":" loop ends at the next suspension point, exactly as it would on teardown."}]},{"type":"heading","text":"Debounce with `cancelInFlight`","level":2,"anchor":"Debounce-with-cancelInFlight"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Passing "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"cancelInFlight: true"},{"type":"text","text":" cancels any effect already running under the id "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"text":"before","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":" starting the new one — the whole of debounce in one line:"}]},{"type":"codeListing","code":["case .queryChanged(let query):","    return cancellable(id: SearchID(), cancelInFlight: true) { send in","        try await Task.sleep(for: .milliseconds(300))","        let results = try await api.search(query)","        await send(.results(results))","    }"],"syntax":"swift"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Each keystroke re-dispatches "},{"code":".queryChanged","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"; the new effect cancels the previous sleeping one, so only the last query in a burst reaches the network."}]},{"type":"heading","text":"Cancel from view or scene code","level":2,"anchor":"Cancel-from-view-or-scene-code"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"When there is no reducer action to hang the cancellation on — a screen disappearing, a sheet dismissing — call "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/Store\/cancel(id:)","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" directly:"}]},{"type":"codeListing","code":[".onDisappear {","    store.cancel(id: SearchID())","}"],"syntax":"swift"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Ids with nothing running are ignored, so it is always safe to call.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"heading","text":"What it does not replace","level":2,"anchor":"What-it-does-not-replace"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Keyed cancellation is not a substitute for resource cleanup. An effect holding a file handle, a network connection, or an "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"AsyncStream"},{"type":"text","text":" continuation should still release it — use "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"withTaskCancellationHandler"},{"type":"text","text":" or a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"defer"},{"type":"text","text":". Cancellation ends the task; it does not close what the task opened."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Effects that terminate on their own (a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"for await"},{"type":"text","text":" loop whose stream finishes) need no id at all. Only reach for a cancel id when something "},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"else"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"type":"text","text":" has to stop the effect early."}]}]}],"sections":[],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Tag an effect with an identity so it can be cancelled later — by another effect, or imperatively from view code."}],"references":{"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/Effect":{"url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/effect","title":"Effect","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"An async unit of work returned by a reducer."}],"kind":"symbol","role":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"Effect"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/Effect","type":"topic","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"typealias"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"Effect"}]},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/HowToAddAPaywall":{"url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/howtoaddapaywall","title":"Add a Paywall","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Wire the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SwiduxPaywall"},{"type":"text","text":" plugin into a Swidux app to gate features behind a subscription or lifetime purchase."}],"kind":"article","role":"article","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/HowToAddAPaywall","type":"topic"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/cancel(id:)":{"url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/cancel(id:)","fragments":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"cancel","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"Action","kind":"genericParameter"},{"text":">(","kind":"text"},{"text":"id","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"some","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Hashable","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:SH"},{"text":" & ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Sendable","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:s8SendableP"},{"text":") -> ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Effect","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:6Swidux6Effecta"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"Action","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":">","kind":"text"}],"type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/cancel(id:)","kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"An effect that cancels every in-flight effect running under "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"id"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"title":"cancel(id:)","role":"symbol"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/HowToAddICloudSync":{"url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/howtoaddicloudsync","title":"Add iCloud Sync","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Layer opt-in, cross-device iCloud sync on top of "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SwiduxPersistence"},{"type":"text","text":" with the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SwiduxCloudKitSync"},{"text":" plugin — including a runtime opt-out toggle, launch-time entitlement detection, and the Apple Developer portal configuration.","type":"text"}],"kind":"article","role":"article","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/HowToAddICloudSync","type":"topic"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/AgentSkill":{"role":"article","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/agentskill","title":"Using the Swidux Agent Skill","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/AgentSkill","type":"topic","kind":"article","abstract":[{"text":"Install the bundled ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"swidux-ref"},{"text":" skill so your AI coding assistant has Swidux’s architecture rules and code templates on hand.","type":"text"}]},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/Store/cancel(id:)":{"url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/store\/cancel(id:)","title":"cancel(id:)","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Cancels every in-flight effect tagged with "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"id"},{"type":"text","text":" via"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/cancellable(id:cancelInFlight:_:)"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"kind":"symbol","role":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/Store\/cancel(id:)","type":"topic","fragments":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"cancel","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"(","kind":"text"},{"text":"id","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"some","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Hashable","preciseIdentifier":"s:SH","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":" & ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Sendable","preciseIdentifier":"s:s8SendableP","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":")","kind":"text"}]},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/HowToAddFeatureFlags":{"url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/howtoaddfeatureflags","title":"Add Feature Flags","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Wire the "},{"code":"SwiduxFeatureFlags","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" plugin into a Swidux app for typed feature flags, A\/B variants, and remote-tunable scalar values from a single JSON config."}],"kind":"article","role":"article","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/HowToAddFeatureFlags","type":"topic"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/BuildingADomainPlugin":{"url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/buildingadomainplugin","title":"Building a Domain Plugin","abstract":[{"text":"Create a self-contained feature plugin with its own state, actions, and effects.","type":"text"}],"kind":"article","role":"article","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/BuildingADomainPlugin","type":"topic"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/HowToAddAParentalGate":{"role":"article","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/howtoaddaparentalgate","title":"Add a Parental Gate","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/HowToAddAParentalGate","type":"topic","kind":"article","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Gate sensitive actions — purchases, settings changes, leaving a kid-mode area — behind a math challenge."}]},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/HowToAddAnalytics":{"url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/howtoaddanalytics","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/HowToAddAnalytics","kind":"article","type":"topic","title":"Add Analytics","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Wire the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SwiduxAnalytics"},{"type":"text","text":" plugin into a Swidux app for centralized event tracking with declarative event mapping and auto-identify."}],"role":"article"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/HowToAddPersistence":{"url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/howtoaddpersistence","title":"Add Persistence","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Persist your domain entities to SwiftData with the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SwiduxPersistence"},{"type":"text","text":" plugin and the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@Persisted"},{"type":"text","text":" macro — no hand-written "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@Model"},{"type":"text","text":" classes, database actors, or "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"StateWriter"},{"type":"text","text":" closures."}],"kind":"article","role":"article","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/HowToAddPersistence","type":"topic"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux":{"role":"collection","url":"\/documentation\/swidux","title":"Swidux","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux","type":"topic","kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Redux-style state management for SwiftUI, with macros for observability and ready-made plugins for persistence, undo, paywalls, version killswitches, and parental gates."}]},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/cancellable(id:cancelInFlight:_:)":{"url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/cancellable(id:cancelinflight:_:)","fragments":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"cancellable","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"Action","kind":"genericParameter"},{"text":">(","kind":"text"},{"text":"id","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"some","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Hashable","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:SH"},{"text":" & ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Sendable","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:s8SendableP"},{"text":", ","kind":"text"},{"text":"cancelInFlight","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Bool","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:Sb"},{"text":", ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Effect","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:6Swidux6Effecta"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"Action","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":">) -> ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Effect","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:6Swidux6Effecta"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"Action","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":">","kind":"text"}],"type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/cancellable(id:cancelInFlight:_:)","kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Tags an effect with a cancellation identity so it can later be cancelled by"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/cancel(id:)","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" or "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Store.cancel(id:)"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"title":"cancellable(id:cancelInFlight:_:)","role":"symbol"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/HowToAddAVersionKillswitch":{"role":"article","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/howtoaddaversionkillswitch","title":"Add a Version Killswitch","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/HowToAddAVersionKillswitch","type":"topic","kind":"article","abstract":[{"text":"Wire a remote-controlled blocker that prevents unsupported app versions from running, with an “Update” path back to the App Store.","type":"text"}]},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/Store/cancelEffects()":{"role":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/store\/canceleffects()","fragments":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"text":"cancelEffects","kind":"identifier"},{"kind":"text","text":"()"}],"title":"cancelEffects()","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/Store\/cancelEffects()","type":"topic","kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Cancels all in-flight effects."}]}}}